   "tool": "finish",
   "args": {
    "summary": "Repaired and successfully generated the finite element model of the 3-span precast small-box girder bridge.\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the accepted decision support.3.dofs set the longitudinal dof of Abutment 3 to \"spring\", but Abutment 3 carries PTFE sliding laminated elastomeric bearings (sliding=true). Per modeling rule MR-03, a PTFE sliding bearing must have longitudinal \"free\" (Kh = 0), exactly like Abutment 0. This inconsistency (spring dof together with Kh = 0) broke the L1/L2/L3 model checks. The decision was revised to {\"vertical\":\"spring\",\"longitudinal\":\"free\",\"rotation\":\"free\"}, matching bearing:3 and the Kh=0 already accepted for support.3.\n\nFinal model: spine_beam_2d, continuous system (no pier column geometry given, so support lines 1 and 2 are bearings on rigid supports per MR-05); 4 small-box girders per span, C50, girder self-weight only. Supports: 0 (abutment, PTFE sliding, longitudinal free), 1 (Pier 1, plain elastomeric fixed, longitudinal spring Kh=26250 kN/m), 2 (Pier 2, PTFE sliding, free), 3 (Abutment 3, PTFE sliding, free); all vertical spring.\n\nKey results (all checks passed):\n- Vertical frequencies: 5.573, 8.426, 10.186 Hz\n- Self-weight support reactions: 820.5 / 2764.1 / 2764.1 / 820.5 kN\n- Self-weight midspan moments: 2690.2 / 2967.7 / 2690.2 kNm; support moments -5649.0 kNm\n- Lane max positive moment 5341.5 kNm, max negative moment -3864.0 kNm\n\nNo unresolved issues."
